# tenfold default key bindings, embedded into the binary (this file is the source).
#
# Format: 10x's key mappings format, `<keys>: <command>` (a space after the colon is required), chords separated
# by a comma, modifiers Control / Shift / Alt, a comma key written Comma. Commands are 10x command names; tenfold's
# own ids (Editor.GotoDefinition) work too.
#
# The first part is 10x's default key map, every binding verbatim from 10x's documentation (KeyMappings), in
# 10x's groups. Commands tenfold does not implement yet stay listed so this file matches 10x; pressing their keys
# shows "not implemented yet: <Command>" (docs/FEATURE_PARITY.md lists them). Up, PageUp, PageDown and Enter appear
# twice in 10x (cursor/editor and autocomplete/rename popups): tenfold files these by the command's context.
# User overrides, later wins: an installed 10x's KeyMappings.10x_settings (setting keys.import10x), then
# <config dir>/tenfold/KeyMappings.10x_settings, then <workspace>/.tenfold/KeyMappings.10x_settings.
# An empty value removes a binding: `Control Q:`

# --- General ---
Control Shift E: ToggleWorkspaceExplorer
Control ': NewTerminal
Control Shift I: ShowTerminal
Control Shift X: ShowCommandPanel
F1: InternetSearch
Control Shift .: ZoomIn
Control Shift Comma: ZoomOut
Alt Enter: ToggleFullscreen
Control Alt Enter: ToggleFocusMode
Shift Alt Enter: ToggleFullScreenFocusMode
Alt X: OpenCurrentFileInDebugger

# --- File ---
Control O: OpenFile
Control F4: CloseFile
Control S: SaveFile
Control S, Control S: SaveAll
Control N: NewTextFile
Control T: ShowInWorkspaceTree
Control Shift Alt /: OpenFolderForActivefile
Control Shift S: SaveAll

