# ===== tenfold additions (not part of 10x's default key map) =====
# Bindings for tenfold commands 10x has no key for. None of these uses a key 10x binds for the same context (Enter
# is 10x's rename-submit key, which lives in the popup context, so the editor's Enter does not clash).

# --- Editing keys the text view handles itself in 10x ---
Backspace: Editor.Backspace
Enter: Editor.Enter
KpEnter: Editor.Enter
Tab: Editor.Tab
Shift Tab: UnindentLine
Escape: Editor.CollapseCarets
Control Backspace: Editor.DeleteWordLeft
Control Delete: Editor.DeleteWordRight
Control /: Editor.ToggleLineComment
Control J: Editor.JoinLines
Control Shift K: DeleteLine

# --- Semantic navigation ---
F12: GotoSymbolDefinition
Control F12: Editor.GotoDeclaration
Shift F12: FindSymbolReferences
Control Comma: FindSymbol

# --- Application, build, debugging, panels ---
Control Q: Exit
Control Shift B: BuildActiveWorkspace
Control Alt O: ToggleBuildOutputPanel
Alt Z: ToggleWordWrap
Control F9: Debug.ToggleBreakpointEnabled
Control F10: Debug.RunToCursor
Control Alt Cancel: Debug.BreakAll
Control Alt B: ListBreakpoints
Alt 1: Workbench.FocusPanel 1
Alt 2: Workbench.FocusPanel 2
Alt 3: Workbench.FocusPanel 3
Alt 4: Workbench.FocusPanel 4

# Debug.EditCondition, Debug.OpenInVisualStudio (10x: OpenCurrentFileInDebugger, Alt X), Build.SelectConfiguration,
# Clangd.Restart, View.ShowDiagnostics, Editor.ListBookmarks, Editor.ToggleBlockComment, Editor.GotoDeclaration and the
# Vcs.* change commands (Vcs.NextChange, Vcs.PrevChange, Vcs.ToggleInlineDiff, Vcs.RevertHunk, Vcs.RefreshStatus) have
# no default key; run them from the command palette or bind them, for example:
# Control Alt V: Vcs.ToggleInlineDiff
